And the fact that they stood up as long as they did was because we had designed the project for the impact of the 707 aircraft and we had a great team working on the project and they did what they were supposed to do. They stood up under the impact. And while it's true that the plane that hit it was a bit heavier and was flying a whole lot faster and therefore a whole lot more energy was put into the building. I think it's a tribute to the people who worked on the project that they did as well as they did. And yet I know, as well as I'm here right this moment, that the buildings could have been made more stoward, sure, they could have been made stronger, and they could have stood up longer.
